2. THE DISCREPANCY

  The ramp check measured sublimation-
  adjusted remaining dry ice at 62%
  of declared quantity at a point
  where flight plan assumptions
  required 85%. Two issues arise
  under IATA DGR:

  a) The DGD's "net quantity per
     package" was carried over from
     the February 2026 template
     (180 kg) while this cycle's
     packing instructions (PI 954)
     call for 215 kg per ULD for
     the GRU sector length;
  b) The Shipper's Declaration
     signature block lacks the
     2027 revision date of the DGR,
     rendering the declaration
     version-invalid for acceptance.

3. WHAT IS REQUIRED

  a) A corrected Shipper's
     Declaration (DGD) on the 2027
     form, quantities restated;
  b) Confirmation from your
     responsible DG officer that
     no other consignments shipped
     this week carry the 2026
     template quantities;
  c) Settlement of the DG
     administrative correction
     fee: EUR 640.00 per ULD
     x 6 = EUR 3,840.00, payable
     to the compliance settlement
     account below BEFORE re-
     acceptance (the fee covers
     re-check, re-documentation
     and ramp re-handling):

       Beneficiary: AFS Compliance
                    Settlements Ltd.
       IBAN: DE44 5001 0517 5407 3216 88
       BIC: TSTBDEFFXXX
       Reference: 176-88412375 / DGR

4. TIMELINE

  - Uplift cutoff: tomorrow night
    22:40 local (FRA), the last
    GRU-compatible cold chain
    departure this week
